---
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const STORAGE_ROWS = [
  { data: "Rosters", local: "Disk", cloud: "Plaintext" },
  { data: "Drafts (member, session ID, timestamps)", local: "Disk", cloud: "Plaintext. Session IDs are random" },
  { data: "Tasks", local: "Disk", cloud: "AES-256-GCM ciphertext" },
  { data: "Repo identity (owner/repo)", local: "Disk", cloud: "HMAC-SHA256 fingerprint" },
  { data: "rostr key", local: "—", cloud: "Never transmitted" },
];

const KEY_DERIVATION = `rostr key
  ├─ HKDF-SHA256(info="auth")        → auth token
  ├─ HKDF-SHA256(info="encrypt")     → encryption key
  └─ HKDF-SHA256(info="fingerprint") → fingerprint key`;
---

<Layout title="rostr privacy" description="How rostr stores, encrypts, and fingerprints your data.">
  <section class="privacy-hero">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Local mode makes no network calls. Cloud mode stores rosters and draft state on the rostr API; tasks and repo
      names are encrypted or fingerprinted on your machine before they're sent.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Data</h2>
    <table class="storage-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Data</th>
          <th>Local</th>
          <th>Cloud (server)</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {STORAGE_ROWS.map((row) => (
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{row.data}</th>
            <td>{row.local}</td>
            <td>{row.cloud}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Keys</h2>
    <p>The CLI derives three independent keys from your rostr key. Only the auth token leaves your machine.</p>
    <Code code={KEY_DERIVATION} lang="text" frame="none" />
    <ul class="terse-list">
      <li><strong>Auth token:</strong> bearer credential for the API. The server stores only its SHA-256 hash.</li>
      <li><strong>Encryption key:</strong> encrypts tasks with AES-256-GCM, with a random 96-bit nonce per task.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Fingerprint key:</strong> HMAC-SHA256 over <code>owner/repo</code>, so the server can match project
        links without learning repo names.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>Distinct HKDF labels make the keys independent: none reveals the rostr key or any other derived key.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>What the server sees</h2>
    <ul class="terse-list">
      <li>
        <strong>Visible:</strong> roster contents, which members are drafted and when, session IDs, repo fingerprints,
        and the size and timing of task ciphertext.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Not visible:</strong> your rostr key, task plaintext, repo names, prompts, or code.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Consequences</h2>
    <ul class="terse-list">
      <li><strong>No recovery.</strong> A lost key means your cloud data is unrecoverable, by you or by us.</li>
      <li><strong>API responses</strong> contain task ciphertext. <code>rostr list --json</code> decrypts it for you.</li>
      <li><strong>Cloud environments</strong> need <code>ROSTR_KEY</code> to decrypt tasks. Never commit it.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy-hero {
    padding: 72px 0 40px;
  }

  .privacy-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(36px, 6vw, 52px);
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }

  .storage-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  .storage-table th,
  .storage-table td {
    padding: 10px 8px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  .storage-table thead th {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }

  .storage-table tbody th {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .storage-table td {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .terse-list {
    margin: 16px 0;
    padding-left: 20px;
    max-width: 44em;
  }

  .terse-list li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
</style>
